WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.368
-Welcome back
to "The Tonight Show"!

00:00:02.368 --> 00:00:03.536
We're hanging out
with Jerry Seinfeld!

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:06.105
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.105 --> 00:00:08.374
This is very exciting.
As of today,

00:00:08.374 --> 00:00:11.977
180 episodes of "Seinfeld"
available on Netflix.

00:00:11.977 --> 00:00:15.081
-Yeah, so that's 200 million
subscribers that they have.

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:18.584
This show has never been out
to that many people before.

00:00:18.584 --> 00:00:20.687
It's really --
So, like, different countries,

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:22.822
different places
that have never seen it.

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:24.858
It's kind of cool.
-Yeah, it's bizarre.

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:26.292
-Yeah.
-I think it's fantastic.

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:28.061
-Yeah, yeah,
I'm very excited about it.

00:00:28.061 --> 00:00:30.896
It's weird to me
that the show is like --

00:00:30.896 --> 00:00:33.132
You did that "Sopranos" joke.
It's true that these shows

00:00:33.132 --> 00:00:36.569
go away, and then
we breed a new audience...

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:37.970
-Yeah.
-...and then it's a new show.

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:39.372
-And this --
But now it's international

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:40.506
'cause Netflix
knows how to do it.

00:00:40.506 --> 00:00:42.408
Yeah.
-Do they dub it?

00:00:42.408 --> 00:00:45.845
Yeah.
So, Uruguay or wherever you are.

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:47.079
There it is.
Very exciting.

00:00:47.079 --> 00:00:50.216
-You know, I also -- I --
When the show was on --

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:54.754
reran locally, I didn't watch
because I was such a superfan

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:56.722
that I was like --
Nancy, my wife,

00:00:56.722 --> 00:00:58.157
watches you all the time.
-Right.

00:00:58.157 --> 00:01:00.226
-And I go,
"I got to take a break.

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:02.061
Because...
-Why?

00:01:02.061 --> 00:01:04.030
-Well, because I --
I start talking.

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:05.765
I start talking like you,
and I --

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:07.466
-[ Laughs ]
-You know?

00:01:07.466 --> 00:01:09.602
And I do that.
Yeah, and I talk like you,

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:11.137
and I do that, and I go --
I can't be --

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:12.671
I have to be me for once,
you know?

00:01:12.671 --> 00:01:14.140
Yeah.
-And so I was me

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:15.508
for the last couple years.

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:17.210
And now I feel, with Netflix,
I'm gonna be you again.

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:18.477
-Now you can go back
to being me. Yeah.

00:01:18.477 --> 00:01:21.247
-Yeah.
But 180 episodes is a lot of TV.

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:22.381
-Yeah, it's a lot.

00:01:22.381 --> 00:01:24.250
We made nine years
worth of shows.

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:26.986
In those days,
you'd make 22, 24 a year.

00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:28.354
-Right.
And great shows.

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:29.822
-Thank you, thank you.
-I don't even know

00:01:29.822 --> 00:01:31.624
if there was a bad one.
Everything was --

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:35.761
-Everything varies in life.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:35.761 --> 00:01:40.132
But I heard that you did
a "Seinfeld" promo on Netflix

00:01:40.132 --> 00:01:41.568
where you were a Lego.

00:01:41.568 --> 00:01:44.970
-Well, what happened is,
the Lego company came out

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:49.408
with a model of the set --
of the the apartment set

00:01:49.408 --> 00:01:50.877
from the series.
-Yeah.

00:01:50.877 --> 00:01:53.913
-And Netflix saying, "Hey, we
need to do a promo for your show

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:55.448
coming on the platform."

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:58.952
And I thought, "What if I
could get in that toy?

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:02.555
I want to get in there somehow."
-Yeah. Of course.

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:04.057
-"Can you get me in there?"
and they said,

00:02:04.057 --> 00:02:06.859
"Yes, we're Netflix.
We can get you in there."

00:02:06.859 --> 00:02:08.227
[ Laughter ]
So they did it.

00:02:08.227 --> 00:02:10.162
They got me in there.
And here it is.

00:02:10.162 --> 00:02:11.764
-Let's check it out.

00:02:11.764 --> 00:02:14.033
-Coming this fall to Netflix,
"Seinfeld"!

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:17.036
It's must-see TV like you've
never seen it before.

00:02:17.036 --> 00:02:22.008
Inspired by the wildly popular
Lego set model!

00:02:22.008 --> 00:02:25.077
it's Lego Seinfeld!
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:25.077 --> 00:02:27.780
He's blocky!
He's stompy!

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.882
He's one half
real organic matter.

00:02:29.882 --> 00:02:32.051
He has C hands!

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:35.154
And he's every bit as funny
as his human counterpart.

00:02:35.154 --> 00:02:37.623
-I am the human counterpart!

00:02:37.623 --> 00:02:40.893
They shrunk me down.
-Quiet!

00:02:40.893 --> 00:02:43.362
-I guess I'll have cereal.

00:02:43.362 --> 00:02:45.264
-His milk never spoils.

00:02:45.264 --> 00:02:50.603 line:0%
♪♪

00:02:50.603 --> 00:02:54.206
His pants clean in one wipe!

00:02:54.206 --> 00:02:57.076
-I don't know what this is.
What are we selling here?

00:02:57.076 --> 00:02:59.612
-Oh, sorry, Jerry.
You have no say.

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:02.949
We bought the series, and we
can do whatever we want with it.

00:03:02.949 --> 00:03:06.152
And you.
-But I don't want to be a Lego!

00:03:09.322 --> 00:03:10.890
[ Loud crunching ]

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:13.459
Pbht! Pbht!

00:03:13.459 --> 00:03:16.262
I don't even know who I'm
working for at this point.

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:19.265
Hello?
Hello?

00:03:19.265 --> 00:03:21.000
This phone is not real.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.202
-Lego Puddy sold separately.
-Yeah, that's right.

00:03:23.202 --> 00:03:24.603
Lego Whatley not available.

00:03:24.603 --> 00:03:27.140
Oh. What happened to Whatley?
He did like five episodes.

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:28.775
-Six!

00:03:28.775 --> 00:03:32.145
-I don't know how this happened,
but I am not a toy.

00:03:32.145 --> 00:03:34.814
-All 180 episodes
only on Netflix.

00:03:34.814 --> 00:03:36.649
[ Cheers and applause ]
Come on!

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:39.018
That is how you do it
right there.

00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:41.521
That is -- That looked --
That looked great!

00:03:41.521 --> 00:03:43.422
-It was fun.
-You were a Lego!

00:03:43.422 --> 00:03:45.391
-Yes, I became a Lego.

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:47.627
-I love that.
I thought that was so --

00:03:47.627 --> 00:03:50.296
Oh, it was perfect.
-Thank you, thank you.

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:54.700
-I -- I heard that you just went
on summer vacation.

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:56.101
-No.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:56.101 --> 00:03:57.770
No, I did not.
-Oh.

00:03:57.770 --> 00:04:00.573
-I don't really like
going on vacations.

00:04:00.573 --> 00:04:02.508
I don't like
that somebody else thinks

00:04:02.508 --> 00:04:05.344
I'm gonna like something.
Just -- Just the idea --

00:04:05.344 --> 00:04:08.247
You go to these places, "Here's
some things you'll love!"

00:04:08.247 --> 00:04:10.249
You know,
the stand-up paddle board.

00:04:10.249 --> 00:04:12.084
-Yeah.
-You know, it's like

00:04:12.084 --> 00:04:14.420
a goldfish comes up and goes,
"Is that your top speed?"

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:18.257
and I go, "Yeah, I'm wide open.
This is it."

00:04:18.257 --> 00:04:20.827
-You know, I can't --
I can't get that the Lego thing

00:04:20.827 --> 00:04:22.194
out of my head, that scene.

00:04:22.194 --> 00:04:24.697
-Yeah, it's kind of
a you bit, isn't it?

00:04:24.697 --> 00:04:27.032
-I would love -- I feel like
I would love to be a Lego.

00:04:27.032 --> 00:04:28.868
-Yeah, I know,
you probably would.

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:30.069
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:31.504
-I mean, it really seems like
my kind of thing.

00:04:31.504 --> 00:04:34.073
-It is kind of -- your kind of
thing, but I already did it.

00:04:34.073 --> 00:04:35.775
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:35.775 --> 00:04:38.844
-I want to be a Lego.
-You want to be Lego?

00:04:38.844 --> 00:04:41.347
-Please?

00:04:41.347 --> 00:04:45.084
-Okay, if you want, I can
take you into the Lego world

00:04:45.084 --> 00:04:46.685
if you want to.
-We can do this?

00:04:46.685 --> 00:04:47.954
-Yes.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:47.954 --> 00:04:49.188
All right.
What do we have to do?

00:04:49.188 --> 00:04:52.191
Come on over here.
-Okay.

00:04:52.191 --> 00:04:54.460
All right.
What do we have to do?

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:57.129
-All right.
Now I want you to...

00:04:57.129 --> 00:05:00.832
say -- you have to say,
"I don't want to be a Lego,"

00:05:00.832 --> 00:05:05.638
but you have to say it
like I said it on the series.

00:05:05.638 --> 00:05:06.939
Remember?
"I don't want to be a pirate."

00:05:06.939 --> 00:05:08.407
-Yeah, of course, yeah.
-Which is --

00:05:08.407 --> 00:05:10.776
That delivery is kind of like
a kid who's been told,

00:05:10.776 --> 00:05:11.978
"This is
your Halloween costume."

00:05:11.978 --> 00:05:13.712
-That's correct.
-And he doesn't like it.

00:05:13.712 --> 00:05:16.014
-Okay.
"I don't want to be a Lego."

00:05:16.014 --> 00:05:17.250
-You know,
you got to get up there.

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:19.852
You know, comedy,
you got to hit those notes.

00:05:19.852 --> 00:05:22.755
-I -- I don't wanna be a --
-I don't want to be a Lego!

00:05:22.755 --> 00:05:24.756
-Higher.
-I don't want to be a Lego!

00:05:24.756 --> 00:05:26.091
[ Laughter ]
-No, no, no.

00:05:26.091 --> 00:05:28.060
Is that too high?
-That's too high.

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:30.363
And then it's --
it's got a down and then up.

00:05:30.363 --> 00:05:32.765
-Okay.
-Want me to do it for you?

00:05:32.765 --> 00:05:34.934
"I don't wanna be a Lego!"
[ Laughter ]

00:05:34.934 --> 00:05:37.670
-"I don't want to be a Lego!"

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:38.904
-That's it.
Okay. You've got it.

00:05:38.904 --> 00:05:40.139
All right. Hold my hand.
-Uh-huh.

00:05:40.139 --> 00:05:42.575
[ Laughter ]

00:05:42.575 --> 00:05:46.645
-I don't want to be a Lego!
I don't want to be a Lego!

00:05:46.645 --> 00:05:48.581
I don't want to be a Lego!

00:05:48.581 --> 00:05:50.383
[ Ting! ]

00:05:50.383 --> 00:05:52.451
Wow!
-Oh, my God!

00:05:52.451 --> 00:05:55.154
-This is so neat.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:55.154 --> 00:05:58.724
It feels so good.

00:05:58.724 --> 00:06:01.693
This is amazing being a Lego!
-This is great!

00:06:01.693 --> 00:06:05.097
-Yes! Well, what do --
what do we do now?

00:06:05.097 --> 00:06:07.800
-Well, let's continue the show.
-Yeah, okay.

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:10.203
All right. Have a seat, please.
-Oh, sure.

00:06:10.203 --> 00:06:12.371
Don't you need your desk?
-I do need my desk.

00:06:12.371 --> 00:06:14.674
-Okay. Well, let me help you
up on the desk.

00:06:14.674 --> 00:06:20.712
[ Laughter ]

00:06:20.712 --> 00:06:21.780
-Well, you got --
[ Grunts ]

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:24.016
You have to...

00:06:24.016 --> 00:06:25.551
[ Laughter ]

00:06:25.551 --> 00:06:28.920
[ Both grunting ]

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:30.890
You got to roll over.

00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:33.926
[ Laughter ]

00:06:36.729 --> 00:06:40.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:46.905 --> 00:06:49.141
-Anyway, you were saying?

00:06:49.141 --> 00:06:52.244
-Uh, yeah,
I was just talking about, um...

00:06:52.244 --> 00:06:56.349
You know, I don't really enjoy
going on vacations that much.

00:06:56.349 --> 00:06:58.216
-Did you get a chance
to get away this summer?

00:06:58.216 --> 00:06:59.985
-I did.
We went on a little trip,

00:06:59.985 --> 00:07:03.455
and -- I don't know.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:03.455 --> 00:07:05.324
I just, uh...

00:07:05.324 --> 00:07:07.160
You know,
the things they have there,

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:09.628
you know, like the zip line.

00:07:09.628 --> 00:07:12.732
It's like, you know, let's risk
decapitation to find out

00:07:12.732 --> 00:07:14.367
what it feels like
to be dry-cleaned.

00:07:14.367 --> 00:07:16.535
[ Laughter ]

00:07:16.535 --> 00:07:18.370
What's the point?
-What is the point?

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:19.939
-Yeah.
And I'm sure if we did

00:07:19.939 --> 00:07:22.108
get seriously hurt
on this thing,

00:07:22.108 --> 00:07:25.010
we'll do very well navigating
the court system

00:07:25.010 --> 00:07:26.812
in this
fifth-world island nation

00:07:26.812 --> 00:07:29.114
that's being run
by Komodo dragons.

00:07:29.114 --> 00:07:30.383
[ Laughter ]
-That is so funny.

00:07:30.383 --> 00:07:32.818
-Oh, thank you.
Thank you.

00:07:32.818 --> 00:07:36.021
[ Legos clattering ]

00:07:36.021 --> 00:07:39.025
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:39.025 --> 00:07:41.661
Pbht!

00:07:41.661 --> 00:07:43.229
-Jerry, could you have
ever imagined

00:07:43.229 --> 00:07:45.230
that when "Seinfeld"
first premiered,

00:07:45.230 --> 00:07:47.099
we'd have things like Netflix,
and you'd be able

00:07:47.099 --> 00:07:49.668
to watch your show,
like, on your phone?

00:07:49.668 --> 00:07:53.238
-No, I could never
imagine such a thing.

00:07:53.238 --> 00:07:54.674
To me, the phone,

00:07:54.674 --> 00:07:58.411
I kind of feel bad
sometimes for Google and Siri,

00:07:58.411 --> 00:08:01.647
'cause they always have to be
so nice, you know?

00:08:01.647 --> 00:08:03.149
"On it!"

00:08:03.149 --> 00:08:05.351
"I'm sorry.
I didn't get that."

00:08:05.351 --> 00:08:06.886
-Yeah.
You know, just once in a while,

00:08:06.886 --> 00:08:10.189
I feel like they should go,
"Really? You don't know that?"

00:08:10.189 --> 00:08:11.690
[ Laughter ]

00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:15.461
"No, no. You rest. I'll get it.
I'll figure it out."

00:08:15.461 --> 00:08:16.695
[ Laughter ]

00:08:16.695 --> 00:08:18.730
Just once
I want to hear Siri go.

00:08:18.730 --> 00:08:20.433
"Why don't you learn
how to enunciate,

00:08:20.433 --> 00:08:22.434
and maybe
we don't have to do this?"

00:08:22.434 --> 00:08:23.469
-That's exactly correct.

00:08:23.469 --> 00:08:25.605
-"Not always my fault,
you know."

00:08:25.605 --> 00:08:28.774
-[ Laughs ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:28.774 --> 00:08:30.242
[ Legos clattering ]

00:08:30.242 --> 00:08:38.284
[ Laughter ]

00:08:38.284 --> 00:08:40.853
Enough water --
Enough water for me.

00:08:40.853 --> 00:08:43.522
[ Laughter ]

00:08:43.522 --> 00:08:44.890
This -- This has been fun,

00:08:44.890 --> 00:08:47.793
but I have other guests
I have to interview.

00:08:47.793 --> 00:08:49.561
-Oh.
-So I think we should get back.

00:08:49.561 --> 00:08:51.897
How do we -- How do we get?
-You want to get back?

00:08:51.897 --> 00:08:53.198
-Yeah.
How do we do it?

00:08:53.198 --> 00:08:55.534
-Um...
I know how.

00:08:55.534 --> 00:08:59.271
Let's stand up.
[ Grunts ]

00:08:59.271 --> 00:09:02.708
[ Laughter ]

00:09:02.708 --> 00:09:05.511
-Ohh! Pfft!
What was that?

00:09:05.511 --> 00:09:08.381
-That was a part of your cup.
-Okay.

00:09:08.381 --> 00:09:10.382
[ Laughter ]
Get that out of -- thank you.

00:09:10.382 --> 00:09:11.817
-Okay.
-Thank you.

00:09:11.817 --> 00:09:13.018
The worst thing is...
-Come on down.

00:09:13.018 --> 00:09:14.686
...when you step on
a Lego barefoot.

00:09:14.686 --> 00:09:15.688
You know what I'm saying?

00:09:15.688 --> 00:09:17.890
[ Laughter ]

00:09:17.890 --> 00:09:19.191
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:19.191 --> 00:09:24.063
-Pfft!
-[ Laughs ]

00:09:24.063 --> 00:09:27.333
Oh, my God.
I had no idea you used a piece.

00:09:27.333 --> 00:09:32.037
[ Laughter ]

00:09:32.037 --> 00:09:34.439
All right.
So, how do we get back?

00:09:34.439 --> 00:09:37.309
-Uh, hold my hand.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:37.309 --> 00:09:41.180
Now just say,
"There's no place like 6B."

00:09:41.180 --> 00:09:45.918
-There's no place like 6B.
There's no place like 6B.

00:09:45.918 --> 00:09:48.320
[ Ting! ]

00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:51.723
-And that's why your spouse
is like a rescue pet.

00:09:51.723 --> 00:09:54.826
[ Laughter and applause ]
Jimmy?

00:09:54.826 --> 00:09:56.162
Jimmy, are you listening to me?

00:09:56.162 --> 00:09:57.596
-Oh, yeah.
Oh, sorry.

00:09:57.596 --> 00:09:59.131
Just never mind.

00:09:59.131 --> 00:10:00.832
But thanks to Jerry Seinfeld,
everybody.

00:10:00.832 --> 00:10:04.570
All episodes of "Seinfeld"
are available on Netflix now!

